WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.920
So the California democratic state convention
happened over the weekend and there were some

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.140
interesting things that happen, including
including a lot of booing of presidential

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.590
candidates. I think you're going to like this.
First of all, there's a guy running named

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:17.890
John Delaney. He was a congressman in Maryland
from 2013 until this year. He's polling almost

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:24.699
zero, I think averaging, yeah, 0.5% to be
exact. So he has no shot, but he showed up

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:31.999
and he said Medicare for all might sound good
but it's not a good policy and it's not good

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:36.960
politics and he got booed so much that it
actually got awkward. Take a look.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:44.320
But we need as Democrats to build an economy
that works, but it's gotta be with smart policies.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:54.460
Medicare for all may sound good, but it's
actually not good policy nor is it good.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:19.350
I'm telling you, I'm telling you a hundred
[inaudible] we should have universal healthcare.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:26.630
We should have universal healthcare. Seriously

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:31.080
awkward moment because the booing just wouldn't
stop. But I'm going to take a position on

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.970
this that I know people are going to miss
here and get angry with me about. But if he

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:40.890
had tweaked what he said slightly, it would
have actually been a really strong statement

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:45.701
with which I'd agree because right now there
is huge momentum over medicare for all. But

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:50.350
as I've said before, medicare for all is just
one way to get universal coverage and healthcare

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:56.960
to everyone. I've said before, I'm a supporter
of Medicare for all over the system. We have,

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:01.870
and I'm a supporter of Medicare for all over
lots of other ideas that have been presented,

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:08.009
uh, including, you know, the public option
as part of Obamacare or whatever else. But

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:12.690
there are problems with Medicare. Medicare
is not nearly a perfect system. Would I take

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.440
it over what we have of course a million times
over.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:20.180
But remember that 80% of the people who are
on Medicare have something else in addition

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:24.920
to Medicare because Medicare doesn't give
them full coverage. Some people are working

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:30.111
while on Medicare, so they have some kind
of private employer connected insurance. Some

00:02:30.111 --> 00:02:34.940
people who have medicare are buying additional
coverage through various supplement plans

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:40.530
or they're poor enough to get Medicaid in
conjunction with Medicare. But the point is

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:45.290
medicare for all isn't perfect. And if Delaney
instead came in and said, listen, instead

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:50.819
of saying Medicare for all is bad politics
and bad policy, instead of saying my top priority

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:57.110
is getting healthcare to everyone as soon
as possible, and I will consider any system

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:03.180
that gets us there, be it medicare for all
a massive medicaid expansion, a nationalization

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.990
type system like in the UK, a state based
system that is similar to what Canada has

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:11.130
at the province level, it doesn't matter.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:16.569
Right. That would actually be a really great
thing to hear from John Delaney because sometimes

00:03:16.569 --> 00:03:22.480
I agree the left gets too, they get blinders
on with Medicare for all when there are other

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:29.540
options and it's a perfectly reasonable debate
to be had to show up and say, Hey, this is

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:35.040
bad policy and bad politics. He's a fool,
he's a fool. And if it's an idiotic way to

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.950
present it, uh, but there is actually a good
discussion in there that we could have, which

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:44.209
is Medicare is not perfect and there are other
countries that have different types of systems

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:49.270
which might be better if implemented in the
United States. And we should consider all

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:53.500
of them. We shouldn't rule any of it out.
I've been talking about that. So huge strategic

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:58.790
mistake by Delaney in a boneheaded way. A
really just putting his foot in his mouth.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:02.760
Then in comes John Hickenlooper at the same
California Democratic convention, another

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:08.620
Democrat running with no support. He's pulling
0.3% Hickenlooper was the governor of Colorado

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:16.590
from 2013 until this year. And he said socialism
is not the answer and he got booed. Let's

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:33.419
take a look at that clip.

00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:49.719
[inaudible] [inaudible] okay.

00:04:49.719 --> 00:04:55.629
And the booing just went on from there. This
is another dumb strategic mistake. I agree

00:04:55.629 --> 00:05:02.189
with Hickenlooper in that for me, socialism
is not the answer. I want, uh, to sort of

00:05:02.189 --> 00:05:07.389
take control of the capitalist system that
we have and tweak and tailor it in the way

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:12.059
that the Nordic countries and other northern
European countries have done. Denmark, Finland,

00:05:12.059 --> 00:05:17.389
whatever. These are capitalist countries that
have said, capitalism only goes so far and

00:05:17.389 --> 00:05:21.430
we need to control it and rate it in for the
benefit of everybody in our country to make

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:26.199
sure people don't get left behind. So I agree
with Hickenlooper. Socialism is not the answer,

00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:31.039
but socialism is a nonstarter, right? I mean,
who's running on the socialization of the

00:05:31.039 --> 00:05:35.080
means of production were workers on every
business and there's no more private ownership

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:38.479
of business. I'm not for that. Nobody's running
on that.

00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:43.449
Right? Why? Why is the guy even attacking
socialism at all? There's no candidates running

00:05:43.449 --> 00:05:48.599
on socialist policies if it's an indirect
attack on Bernie. Okay. Bernie is running

00:05:48.599 --> 00:05:54.330
on social democratic ideas like what we see
in countries like Denmark in those other countries.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:06:00.300
When Trump yelled at his state of the Union
speech, we will never be a socialist country.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:05.360
And the Republican's clapped and went crazy
and some republicans did too. I pointed out

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:11.590
this is idiotic red meat because there is
no serious risk that the United States is

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:17.699
going to become a socialist country. The Democratic
Party has almost no socialists in it. Uh,

00:06:17.699 --> 00:06:21.639
it's a straw man. It's a complete and total
straw man. And similarly, when Hickenlooper

00:06:21.639 --> 00:06:27.659
shows up and says, socialism is not the answer,
who's he talking to? Like, okay, there were

00:06:27.659 --> 00:06:32.909
some people in the crowd who didn't like it.
I would bet that even most of those people

00:06:32.909 --> 00:06:36.639
who think that they're socialists are actually
social democrats.

00:06:36.639 --> 00:06:41.039
I know there are real socialists in the u
s a lot of them don't even understand that

00:06:41.039 --> 00:06:46.539
they're actually social democrats. This is
yet another one of these dumb strategic mistakes.

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:51.279
Not that it matters for Hickenlooper because
the guy has absolutely no shot. Talk about

00:06:51.279 --> 00:06:57.550
what you're for rather than socialism is not
the answer because who's talking about socialism?

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:04.180
I know that in some polls, socialism is less
unfavorably scene than it has been in a long

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:09.779
time. Again, many of those people are talking
about social democracy, but more importantly,

00:07:09.779 --> 00:07:15.069
even if socialism is less unpopular than it
has been in a long time, which I agree it

00:07:15.069 --> 00:07:19.580
is. I mean it's clear from the polls that
that that's the case. Socialism has been sort

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:25.990
of reinvigorated in some sense. We're not
fighting socialism. The Democratic primary

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:33.119
is not a socialism versus capitalism primary.
It's a how regulated of a capitalist system

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:40.830
are we arguing that we should have? How much
of the value created by capitalism do we believe

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:46.699
should be assigned to improving society? And
the economy for everyone, regardless of their

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:50.960
ability to pay on their economic circumstances.
He's having a debate with effectively nobody

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:55.909
when it comes to the content of the Democratic
Party, a party, dumb move, dumb move by Hickenlooper

00:07:55.909 --> 00:07:58.909
and Delaney. But very little risks since neither
of them.

00:07:58.909 --> 00:08:02.659
And have a shot my misinterpreting this. Let
me know what you think. Make sure to give

